foundation.solution_text:
All four sides carry the same tick and all four angles are right angles, so the shape is a square.
The right angles force both pairs of opposite sides to be parallel, so it is a parallelogram, and with four right angles it is a rectangle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.75]
\tikzset{tk/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw (0pt,-4pt)--(0pt,4pt);}}}},tkk/.style={postaction={decorate,decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\draw (-2.5pt,-4pt)--(-2.5pt,4pt);\draw (2.5pt,-4pt)--(2.5pt,4pt);}}}}}
\draw[tk] (0,0)--(3.4,0);
\draw[tk] (3.4,0)--(3.4,3.4);
\draw[tk] (3.4,3.4)--(0,3.4);
\draw[tk] (0,3.4)--(0,0);
\draw (0.32,0)--(0.32,0.32)--(0,0.32);
\draw (3.4,0.32)--(3.08,0.32)--(3.08,0);
\draw (3.08,3.4)--(3.08,3.08)--(3.4,3.08);
\draw (0,3.08)--(0.32,3.08)--(0.32,3.4);
\draw[->] (1.5,0)--(1.9,0);
\draw[->] (1.5,3.4)--(1.9,3.4);
\draw[->] (0,1.1)--(0,1.5);
\draw[->] (0,1.6)--(0,2.0);
\draw[->] (3.4,1.1)--(3.4,1.5);
\draw[->] (3.4,1.6)--(3.4,2.0);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Four equal sides make it a rhombus, and four equal sides also give two pairs of equal adjacent sides, which makes it a kite.
Quadrilateral, kite, parallelogram, rhombus, rectangle, square

